      "help": "WHO-HAEM5 recognises four primary splenic B-cell lymphomas/leukaemias (SMZL, HCL, SDRPL and SBLPN — the latter absorbing former HCL-variant and CD5- B-PLL).",
      "reference": {
        "title": "WHO-HAEM5 splenic lymphoma & leukaemia reference gallery",
        "intro": "Open-licence photomicrographs and WHO-HAEM5 compartment/immunophenotype discriminators for primary and secondary splenic lymphoid neoplasms.",
        "columns": 2,
        "groups": [
          {
            "heading": "Splenic marginal zone lymphoma (SMZL)",
            "points": [
              "White pulp-predominant expansion with biphasic targetoid nodules (inner small dark lymphocytes + outer pale marginal zone cells) and secondary red pulp cord/sinus involvement",
              "CD20+, PAX5+, BCL2+, IgM+/IgD+; typically CD5-, CD10-, BCL6-, Cyclin D1-, CD23-, Annexin A1-, CD25-, CD103-",
              "Hilar lymph nodes frequently involved; watch for large-cell transformation to DLBCL"
            ],
            "images": [
              {
                "src": "assets/reference/spleen_lymphoma/smzl_he.jpg",
                "caption": "SMZL — splenic parenchyma showing nodular white pulp expansion with marginal zone pattern and red pulp infiltration (H&E).",
                "credit": "Cureus 2026 (PMC12867676), Fig 4",
                "license": "CC BY 4.0",
                "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12867676/"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "heading": "Hairy cell leukaemia (HCL)",
            "points": [
              "Diffuse red pulp expansion with white pulp atrophy and classic RBC-filled pseudosinuses ('blood lakes') lined by widely spaced lymphoid cells with abundant pale cytoplasm ('fried-egg' appearance)",
              "CD20+, Annexin A1+, CD25+, CD103+, CD123+, DBA.44+, Cyclin D1 (weak/variable)+",
              "BRAF p.V600E mutated in >95% of cases (distinguishes classic HCL from SBLPN and SDRPL)"
            ],
            "images": [
              {
                "src": "assets/reference/spleen_lymphoma/hcl_spleen_braf.jpg",
                "caption": "HCL in spleen — diffuse red pulp infiltration with strong BRAF V600E mutant protein expression by immunohistochemistry.",
                "credit": "Kim et al., J Hematol 2025 (PMC12151096), Fig 4",
                "license": "CC BY-NC 4.0",
                "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12151096/"
              },
              {
                "src": "assets/reference/spleen_lymphoma/hcl_smear.jpg",
                "caption": "Hairy cell leukaemia — characteristic circulating lymphoid cells with fine circumferential cytoplasmic ('hairy') projections.",
                "credit": "Prof Osaro Erhabor (Wikimedia Commons)",
                "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
                "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hairy_Cell_Leukaemia_(HCL).jpg"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "heading": "Splenic diffuse red pulp small B-cell lymphoma (SDRPL) & SBLPN",
            "points": [
              "SDRPL: diffuse monotonous infiltration of splenic red pulp cords and sinusoids with white pulp atrophy and blood lakes; small-to-medium cells with condensed chromatin and absent/inconspicuous nucleoli; CD20+, DBA.44+, IgG+; negative for Annexin A1, CD25, CD123, Cyclin D1 and BRAF V600E",
              "SBLPN (WHO-HAEM5): absorbs former HCL-variant and CD5- B-PLL; red pulp infiltrate of medium-to-large cells with a prominent single central nucleolus; CD20+, CD11c+, CD103+, DBA.44+; negative for CD25, Annexin A1, CD123 and BRAF V600E; ~50% MAP2K1 mutated"
            ],
            "images": [
              {
                "src": "assets/reference/spleen_lymphoma/sdrpl_cd20.jpg",
                "caption": "SDRPL — intrasinusoidal B-cell infiltration highlighted by CD20 immunohistochemistry (negative for Cyclin D1 and BRAF V600E).",
                "credit": "Genes (Basel) 2025 (PMC12027168), Fig 3a",
                "license": "CC BY 4.0",
                "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12027168/"
              },
              {
                "src": "assets/reference/spleen_lymphoma/sdrpl_smear.jpg",
                "caption": "SDRPL — peripheral blood smear showing small-to-medium lymphoid cells with oval nuclei, condensed chromatin and polar villous projections.",
                "credit": "Genes (Basel) 2025 (PMC12027168), Fig 1",
                "license": "CC BY 4.0",
                "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12027168/"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "heading": "Hepatosplenic T-cell lymphoma (HSTCL)",
            "points": [
              "Marked red pulp expansion with intrasinusoidal and cordal infiltration by monotonous medium-sized lymphoid cells; white pulp is atrophic",
              "Typically CD3+, CD2+, CD7+, TIA-1+, TCR-gamma/delta+ (less often alpha/beta+), CD56+/-; characteristically CD4-/CD8- (double negative), CD5- and Granzyme B-/Perforin- (non-activated cytotoxic phenotype)",
              "Isochromosome 7q [i(7q)] and trisomy 8 are recurrent cytogenetic abnormalities"
            ],
            "images": [
              {
                "src": "assets/reference/spleen_lymphoma/hstcl_he.jpg",
                "caption": "HSTCL — expanded splenic red pulp infiltrated by a monotonous population of medium-sized atypical lymphoid cells (H&E).",
                "credit": "Ammad Ud Din et al., Cureus 2020 (PMC7402550), Fig 2",
                "license": "CC BY 4.0",
                "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7402550/"
              },
              {
                "src": "assets/reference/spleen_lymphoma/hstcl_cd3_cd5.jpg",
                "caption": "HSTCL — strong CD3 positivity (right) with characteristic loss of CD5 expression (left).",
                "credit": "Ammad Ud Din et al., Cureus 2020 (PMC7402550), Fig 3",
                "license": "CC BY 4.0",
                "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7402550/"
              },
              {
                "src": "assets/reference/spleen_lymphoma/hstcl_tia1.jpg",
                "caption": "HSTCL — strong cytoplasmic granular positivity for TIA-1 in sinusoidal/red pulp neoplastic T cells.",
                "credit": "Ammad Ud Din et al., Cureus 2020 (PMC7402550), Fig 4",
                "license": "CC BY 4.0",
                "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7402550/"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "heading": "Primary / secondary splenic follicular lymphoma & DLBCL",
            "points": [
              "Splenic FL: closely packed white pulp neoplastic follicles lacking mantle zones and polarisation; CD20+, CD10+, BCL6+, BCL2+ (inappropriate germinal centre expression)",
              "Splenic DLBCL: typically forms single or multiple large fleshy tan destructive masses with coagulative necrosis; CD20+, high Ki-67"
            ],
            "images": [
              {
                "src": "assets/reference/spleen_lymphoma/fl_spleen_he.jpg",
                "caption": "Primary splenic follicular lymphoma — crowded neoplastic white pulp follicles lacking mantle zones and polarisation (H&E, 100x).",
                "credit": "Cureus 2025 (PMC12576758), Fig 2",
                "license": "CC BY 4.0",
                "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12576758/"
              },
              {
                "src": "assets/reference/spleen_lymphoma/fl_spleen_ihc.jpg",
                "caption": "Primary splenic follicular lymphoma — CD20+ neoplastic follicles (A) with diffuse BCL2 positivity (B) and low Ki-67 ~20% (C).",
                "credit": "Cureus 2025 (PMC12576758), Fig 3",
                "license": "CC BY 4.0",
                "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12576758/"
              },
              {
                "src": "assets/reference/spleen_lymphoma/dlbcl_gross.jpg",
                "caption": "Splenic diffuse large B-cell lymphoma — cut surface showing large confluent fleshy tan tumour masses replacing parenchyma (gross).",
                "credit": "Ed Uthman (Wikimedia Commons)",
                "license": "CC BY 2.0",
                "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Spleen,_Diffuse_Large_B_Cell_Lymphoma_(9187421536).jpg"
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "note": "WHO-HAEM5 splenic lymphoma classification (Alaggio et al., Leukemia 2022, PMC9214472). Click any thumbnail to enlarge."
      }
    },
