      "id": "sblpnNote",
      "label": "SBLPN WHO-HAEM5 terminology note",
      "when": "sblpn",
      "text": "Splenic B-cell lymphoma/leukaemia with prominent nucleoli (SBLPN) is a WHO-HAEM5 entity encompassing cases previously classified as hairy cell leukaemia variant (HCL-v) and CD5-negative B-cell prolymphocytic leukaemia. Correlation with peripheral blood morphology, bone marrow biopsy and molecular testing (BRAF wild-type; MAP2K1 / TP53) is recommended."
    },
    {
      "id": "sdrplNote",
      "label": "SDRPL correlation note",
      "when": "sdrpl",
      "text": "Splenic diffuse red pulp small B-cell lymphoma (SDRPL) is a rare indolent splenic B-cell neoplasm distinguished from hairy cell leukaemia by the absence of CD25, CD123, Annexin A1 and BRAF p.V600E. Correlation with peripheral blood and bone marrow findings is recommended."
    },
    {
      "id": "hstclNote",
      "label": "HSTCL cytogenetics / marrow note",
      "when": "hstcl",
      "text": "Hepatosplenic T-cell lymphoma (HSTCL) is an aggressive extranodal T-cell lymphoma. Cytogenetic/FISH testing for isochromosome 7q [i(7q)] and trisomy 8, together with bone marrow staging, is recommended."
    },
